socket2: IPv6 multicast join/leave on QNX.

socket2 0.5 leaves join_multicast_v6()/leave_multicast_v6() out on QNX
because it imports IPV6_ADD_MEMBERSHIP/IPV6_DROP_MEMBERSHIP, names QNX does
not use. QNX has the BSD names, IPV6_JOIN_GROUP/IPV6_LEAVE_GROUP (12/13 in
<netinet6/in6.h>, exported by libc), so alias them as socket2 already does
for the BSDs, and build the two functions. zenoh-link-udp calls them.

socket2 upstream has QNX in that IPV6_JOIN_GROUP alias list since; the two
functions are still left out for QNX in 0.5.10 and 0.6. Applied to 0.5.10,
the version zenoh-c's and zenohd's Cargo.lock pin for zenoh-link-udp, by
ports/zenoh-c/recipe.sh (socket2 0.6, used by tokio and quinn-udp, needs
nothing).

Upstream-Status: Pending (the alias is upstream, the two functions are not)

